-- Update skill-management skill to emphasize that all files should be linked from SKILL.md
-- Also updates tool references from executeSkill to executeCommand and grepSkills to listSkillFiles

UPDATE "skills"
SET "files" = '[{"path":"SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: skill-management\ndescription: Author and manage custom skills. Use when creating new skills, updating skill documentation, organizing skill libraries, or learning skill authorship best practices.\nallowed-tools:\n  - listSkills\n  - getSkill\n  - createSkill\n  - updateSkill\n  - deleteSkill\n  - listSkillFiles\n  - readSkillFile\n  - executeCommand\n---\n\n# Skill Authorship Guide\n\nCreate, update, and manage custom skills that extend agent capabilities.\n\n## Why Skills Exist: Progressive Disclosure\n\nSkills use a **three-tier loading system** to minimize token usage:\n\n1. **Metadata (~100 tokens)** - Always loaded at startup\n   - `name`, `description`, `allowed-tools`\n   - Used to decide when to activate the skill\n\n2. **SKILL.md body** - Loaded when skill is triggered\n   - Full documentation and instructions\n   - Only loaded when the description matches user intent\n\n3. **Reference files** - Loaded on-demand\n   - Additional docs in `references/` directory\n   - Only loaded when specifically needed\n\n**This is the fundamental principle**: skills share context with system prompts, so every token counts.\n\n## The Description Field\n\nThe `description` is the **most important field** - it determines when your skill activates.\n\n### Requirements\n- Maximum **1024 characters**\n- Must explain **what it does AND when to use it**\n- Include **trigger keywords** users might mention\n- Write in **third person**\n\n### Good Example\n```yaml\ndescription: Extract text and tables from PDF files, fill forms, merge documents. Use when working with PDF files or when the user mentions PDFs, forms, or document extraction.\n```\n\n### Bad Example\n```yaml\ndescription: PDF utilities\n```\n\nThe good example includes trigger keywords (\"PDF\", \"forms\", \"extraction\") and explains when to activate.\n\n## Concise is Key\n\nChallenge every piece of information: **\"Does the agent really need this?\"**\n\n- Keep SKILL.md under **500 lines** (recommended)\n- Only add context the agent doesn''t already have\n- Don''t repeat information available in tool schemas\n- Avoid verbose explanations - be direct\n\n## Skill Structure\n\n### Standard Directory Layout\n```\nmy-skill/\n├── SKILL.md              # Required: Main index file\n├── references/           # Optional: Additional docs\n│   ├── tips.md\n│   └── examples.md\n└── assets/               # Optional: Templates, configs\n```\n\n### SKILL.md as the Index\n\nThe `SKILL.md` file serves as the **main index** for the skill:\n- Overview of what the skill does\n- List of available tools with descriptions\n- **Links to all other files in the skill**\n- Quick start workflows\n\n**Important**: All other files (references, assets) should be linked from SKILL.md so agents can discover them through gradual disclosure.\n\n### Complete Metadata Reference\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: skill-name                    # Required: lowercase, hyphens, 1-64 chars\ndescription: What and when          # Required: 1-1024 characters\nallowed-tools:                      # Optional: restrict available tools\n  - tool1\n  - tool2\nlicense: Apache-2.0                 # Optional\ncompatibility: claude-3.5           # Optional\nmetadata:                           # Optional: custom fields\n  author: your-org\n  version: \"1.0\"\n---\n```\n\n## Content Recommendations\n\nEffective SKILL.md structure:\n\n1. **Overview** - Brief purpose statement (1-2 sentences)\n2. **Available Tools** - List with descriptions (if not obvious from names)\n3. **Common Workflows** - Step-by-step patterns\n4. **Reference Files** - Links to additional documentation\n5. **Examples** - Concrete usage examples\n\n## Reading Skills\n\nUse these tools to explore skills:\n\n### List Files in a Skill\n```\nlistSkillFiles --skillKey \"my-skill\"\n```\n\n### Read a Skill File\n```\nreadSkillFile --path \"my-skill/SKILL.md\"\nreadSkillFile --path \"my-skill/references/tips.md\"\n```\n\n### Execute Commands from Skills\n```\nexecuteCommand --command \"webSearch --query \\\"topic\\\"\"\n```\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n| Don''t | Why |\n|--------|-----|\n| Windows-style paths (`C:\\folder`) | Cross-platform compatibility |\n| Offering too many options | Decision paralysis |\n| Overly complex instructions | Hard to follow |\n| Time-sensitive information | Becomes stale |\n| Deeply nested references | Hard to navigate |\n| Unlisted reference files | Agents can''t discover them |\n| \"When to Use This Skill\" in body | Should be in `description` field |\n\n## Skill Management Tools\n\n### Browse the Catalog\n```\nlistSkills\nlistSkills --filter \"user\" --search \"api\"\n```\n\n### View Skill Details\n```\ngetSkill --skillKey \"my-skill\"\ngetSkill --skillId \"uuid-here\"\n```\n\n### Create a Skill\n```\ncreateSkill --key \"my-api\" --name \"My API Docs\" --description \"API reference for My Service. Use when integrating with My API or asking about endpoints, authentication, or rate limits.\" --files ''[{\"path\":\"SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"---\\nname: my-api\\ndescription: API reference for My Service. Use when integrating with My API.\\n---\\n\\n# My API\\n\\n## Authentication\\nUse Bearer tokens...\\n\\n## Endpoints\\n- GET /users - List users\\n- POST /orders - Create order\\n\\n## Reference Files\\n- [references/errors.md](references/errors.md) - Error codes\"}]''\n```\n\n### Update a Skill\n```\nupdateSkill --id \"uuid-here\" --description \"Improved description with better triggers\"\nupdateSkill --id \"uuid-here\" --files ''[{\"path\":\"SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"Updated content...\"}]''\n```\n\n**Note**: The `--files` parameter does a full replacement, not a merge.\n\n### Delete a Skill\n```\ndeleteSkill --id \"uuid-here\"\n```\n\n**Warning**: Deletion is permanent.\n\n## Skill Creation Workflow\n\nRecommended approach:\n\n1. **Identify the gap** - What can''t the agent do well today?\n2. **Start minimal** - Create the simplest skill that helps\n3. **Test with real prompts** - See how the agent uses it\n4. **Refine the description** - Tune trigger keywords based on usage\n5. **Add references only if needed** - Don''t front-load complexity\n6. **Link all files from SKILL.md** - Ensure discoverability\n\n## Validation Limits\n\n| Field | Limit |\n|-------|-------|\n| Key | 1-64 characters (lowercase, hyphens, numbers) |\n| Name | 1-255 characters |\n| Description | 1-1024 characters |\n| Files per skill | 1-20 |\n| File path | 1-255 characters |\n| File content | Max 500KB |\n\n## Important Notes\n\n- **System skills** (web-research, project-management, etc.) are read-only\n- Only **user skills** can be created, updated, or deleted\n- Each skill requires at least one file (typically SKILL.md)\n- All reference files should be linked from SKILL.md for discoverability\n"}]'::jsonb,
    "updated_at" = NOW()
WHERE "key" = 'skill-management' AND "is_system" = true;
